WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.134 --> 00:00:02.550
CHRISTOPHER SANSON: With almost
500 sessions at Next 2018,

00:00:02.550 --> 00:00:04.799
it's understandable that you
couldn't get to them all.

00:00:04.799 --> 00:00:07.464
So if you didn't see CI/CD
in a Serverless World,

00:00:07.464 --> 00:00:09.255
then stay tuned, because
here's the Rewind.

00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:19.210
The development ecosystem is
always changing for companies

00:00:19.210 --> 00:00:21.520
as they look to grow and
scale their businesses.

00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:25.159
Continuous integration and
continuous delivery, or CI/CD,

00:00:25.159 --> 00:00:26.950
has become an essential
process for helping

00:00:26.950 --> 00:00:30.130
teams deliver code changes
more frequently and reliably.

00:00:30.130 --> 00:00:32.049
Thanks to increases in
serverless technology,

00:00:32.049 --> 00:00:33.590
teams can build and
deploy their code

00:00:33.590 --> 00:00:35.830
with even more
speed and structure.

00:00:35.830 --> 00:00:38.860
First, let's define what
we mean by serverless.

00:00:38.860 --> 00:00:40.780
The core idea here is
that we're able to focus

00:00:40.780 --> 00:00:42.915
on running our application
code without having

00:00:42.915 --> 00:00:44.290
to worry about
the infrastructure

00:00:44.290 --> 00:00:47.710
or the underlying logic used to
run or scale our application.

00:00:47.710 --> 00:00:49.930
Serverless options are
increasing in popularity

00:00:49.930 --> 00:00:53.030
and tools around these are still
evolving and growing rapidly.

00:00:53.030 --> 00:00:55.720
In fact, Google has had a number
of serverless offerings going

00:00:55.720 --> 00:00:58.720
as far back as App Engine,
which released 10 years ago.

00:00:58.720 --> 00:01:01.000
All of these cover a
wide variety of services,

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:03.520
but for CI/CD, we'll
mainly be focusing

00:01:03.520 --> 00:01:07.360
on compute offerings such as
App Engine or Cloud Functions.

00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:09.400
So when looking
at CI/CD, there's

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:12.029
a whole bunch of things like
build agents and configuration

00:01:12.029 --> 00:01:13.570
management that we
would need to deal

00:01:13.570 --> 00:01:15.164
with in a legacy environment.

00:01:15.164 --> 00:01:17.830
Instead of jumping through hoops
and managing the infrastructure

00:01:17.830 --> 00:01:20.860
for all of these, let's focus
on embracing serverless concepts

00:01:20.860 --> 00:01:22.240
and best practices.

00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:24.100
By doing this, we can
reduce our overhead

00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:26.607
and spend more time
on our application.

00:01:26.607 --> 00:01:28.690
Serverless lets us focus
on making our deployments

00:01:28.690 --> 00:01:31.050
automatic, faster, and safer.

00:01:31.050 --> 00:01:33.910
By really drilling into the
automated tasks and process,

00:01:33.910 --> 00:01:36.610
our code can quickly go
from commit to deployed.

00:01:36.610 --> 00:01:39.580
And we're able to customize
build steps such as testing

00:01:39.580 --> 00:01:41.110
and manual approval.

00:01:41.110 --> 00:01:43.660
To capture all the benefits of
coding in a serverless world,

00:01:43.660 --> 00:01:46.340
we can configure tasks and
deployment strategies as needed

00:01:46.340 --> 00:01:48.820
such as blue green and canary.

00:01:48.820 --> 00:01:50.595
For all the processes
we've just outlined,

00:01:50.595 --> 00:01:51.970
we need to tool
to manage all the

00:01:51.970 --> 00:01:53.840
traveling that our
code needs to do,

00:01:53.840 --> 00:01:55.780
and that's where
Cloud Build comes in.

00:01:55.780 --> 00:01:57.520
This is a pretty
typical workflow,

00:01:57.520 --> 00:02:00.070
and Cloud Build helps
improve developer velocity

00:02:00.070 --> 00:02:02.950
and manage the build steps
like packaging and testing,

00:02:02.950 --> 00:02:05.410
deploying to staging, and
reviewing it before finally

00:02:05.410 --> 00:02:07.478
promoting it into production.

00:02:07.478 --> 00:02:08.202
Whew!

00:02:08.202 --> 00:02:09.910
Cloud Build is also
serverless and highly

00:02:09.910 --> 00:02:12.310
configurable with built-in
support for CLI tools,

00:02:12.310 --> 00:02:15.710
encryption for API secrets,
and local build support.

00:02:15.710 --> 00:02:17.330
Whether building on
VMs or serverless,

00:02:17.330 --> 00:02:19.930
a well-structured
CI/CD pipeline lets

00:02:19.930 --> 00:02:21.610
us benefit from automation.

00:02:21.610 --> 00:02:23.890
Cloud Build helps us create
the rules of the system

00:02:23.890 --> 00:02:25.690
and get all the
efficiencies without having

00:02:25.690 --> 00:02:28.150
to worry about any of the
details of the infrastructure.

00:02:28.150 --> 00:02:29.950
In the talk, Christopher
Sanson takes us

00:02:29.950 --> 00:02:31.810
through a demonstration
of his new Prepster

00:02:31.810 --> 00:02:34.907
Shop built on App Engine,
Firebase, and Cloud functions.

00:02:34.907 --> 00:02:36.490
I definitely recommend
checking it out

00:02:36.490 --> 00:02:38.500
to see all the features
of Cloud Build in action

00:02:38.500 --> 00:02:42.052
and how it really enables
CI/CD in a serverless world.

00:02:42.052 --> 00:02:43.510
If you'd like to
see the full talk,

00:02:43.510 --> 00:02:45.350
check out the link in
the description below.

00:02:45.350 --> 00:02:47.433
And don't forget to subscribe
to the Cloud YouTube

00:02:47.433 --> 00:02:49.910
channel for more great
Next Rewind content.

00:02:49.910 --> 00:02:51.660
Thanks for watching.

